emerge_transfer -- sharing is a GENE, and TRANSFER is what pays for it
motif K=3 planted at 1 of 10 positions; train on 3 positions, test on the other 7.
max-pool readout (position never reaches the output). energy = params/(21*10):
  shared = taps, unshared = taps*10. objective = heldout_acc - 1.00*energy.
20 seeds x 200 epochs. GA: pop 24, 50 gens, flips offsets AND the sharing gene.

  producer                    taps  shared contig train acc   heldout  objective
  ideal conv (shared)          3.0    1.00   1.00     0.940     0.912     0.8979
  ideal support, UNSHARED      3.0    0.00   1.00     0.956     0.494     0.3506
  full support (shared)       21.0    1.00   1.00     0.985     0.843     0.7429
  tap-matched random           3.0    1.00   0.00     0.808     0.713     0.6990
  full support, UNSHARED      21.0    0.00   1.00     0.998     0.499    -0.5014
  GA (searches both)           3.0    1.00   0.50     0.984     0.864     0.8498

GATE (protocol item 9, before any operator work):
  PASS if 'ideal conv (shared)' has the highest objective -- the convolution is finally the
  optimum, and the search question becomes meaningful.
  The UNSHARED rows are the mechanism check: they should fit train and collapse on heldout.
  If they transfer too, the task does not demand sharing and this probe is not yet valid.
